      "id": "10f22c9f",
      "agent_input": "Please read docs/q3_report.md and data/sales_q3.csv, then compare the Q3 new contract value in the report to the total of won deals for James Okafor and Sofia Delgado. Let me know if the report needs to be updated.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here are the results of my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Q3 Report vs. CSV Data Comparison\n\n### What the report says\nThe Q3 report (`q3_report.md`) states the new contract value is **$1,040,000** (mentioned in both the Executive Summary and Sales Performance sections).\n\n### What the CSV data shows\nFrom `sales_q3.csv`, the **won deals for James Okafor and Sofia Delgado** are:\n\n| Rep | Deal | Amount |\n|---|---|---|\n| James Okafor | D001 | $87,500 |\n| James Okafor | D003 | $43,000 |\n| James Okafor | D006 | $120,000 |\n| James Okafor | D009 | $95,000 |\n| James Okafor | D012 | $66,000 |\n| James Okafor | D015 | $88,000 |\n| James Okafor | D017 | $72,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D002 | $62,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D005 | $55,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D008 | $38,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D010 | $74,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D019 | $198,000 |\n| Sofia Delgado | D021 | $33,000 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **$1,031,500** |\n\nMarcus Webb also has **one** won deal (D014: $8,500), bringing the **total across all reps** to **$1,040,000** \u2014 which matches the report.\n\n### Verdict: The report does **not** need to be updated\n\nThe report's **$1,040,000** figure is the total new contract value across the **entire team** (Okafor + Delgado + Webb), and it is **correct** when checked against the CSV. The combined won-deal total for just James Okafor and Sofia Delgado is $1,031,500, with the remaining $8,500 coming from Marcus Webb's single won deal (D014). Everything adds up.",
        "status_code": null
      },
