          "tool_output": "# Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across our 15-person team we\nclosed 14 deals out of 22 opportunities, generating **$1,040,000** in new\ncontract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals in the\npending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with critical issues resolved\nsame-day in all cases.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\nTotal closed revenue for the quarter reached **$1,040,000**, with the **South**\nregion leading all territories at **$468,000** in won deals. Our three-person\nfield sales team \u2014 James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb \u2014 collectively worked\n22 active opportunities during the period.\n\nProduct mix shifted toward Meridian Insights Pro, which accounted for the majority of\nclosed revenue. Meridian DataBridge continues to serve as a strong land-and-expand vehicle\nwith several upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\nWin rate for the quarter stood at **63.6%**, slightly above the company\ntarget of 55%. Three deals totalling approximately $240,000 remain in pending status and\nare expected to close by end of September.\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a $198,000 Meridian Insights Pro contract with a\n  Southern-region enterprise customer on September 5 (D019).\n- **Team headcount:** Meridian Analytics closes Q3 at 15 employees across five departments:\n  Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), and Finance (2).\n- **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) were resolved\n  within 24 hours of creation.\n- **License utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) is at 94% capacity \u2014 a\n  procurement review is scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Close the three pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end.\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target $1.2M in new ARR.\n3. Resolve the open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly\n   customer success calls.\n4. Conduct a license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support Q4 roadmap.\n",
          "agent_thought": null
        },
